  "description": "XAFDUD crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H88 Ce6 Mo4 N12 O62 2+,2(C20 H40 Ce3 Mo2 N8 O35 1-),11(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 10 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mo1 (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; Mo2 (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; Ce3A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mo1A (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mo2A (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 10 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 10 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 10 O neighbors; Mo3 (Mo) has 3 O neighbors; Mo4 (Mo) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.041-5.269 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 124.94-163.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [C40H88Ce6Mo4N12O62]2+[C20H40Ce3Mo2N8O35]2·11(C4H8O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 2+.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
